From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:17:55 -0500
Subject: feat: a page after an Arc import says where everything went

An Arc import counted what came across in one line and said nothing of where it
went. Every way into the import now ends on one page, in a new tab of the window:
chrome://stedding-welcome/from_arc.html, "Where everything from Arc went". For
each thing Arc had it gives Arc's word, Stedding's word and a line on how it
works here, with a Show button to the card of Settings where there is one, from
the map on the site's page for people leaving Arc. Under that it says what did
not come across: routes, per-Space profiles, split views and archived tabs, and
what Stedding has nothing like (import I47).

ImportFromArcAsync is where the three entry points meet, so the page opens once
per import from there. A page still open is brought forward and read again, and
an import that found nothing to read opens none. From the welcome flow it waits
behind the dialog, and the flow goes on where it was (welcome W20).

The page is a second page of the welcome WebUI with the flow's stylesheet and a
small one of its own, which lets it scroll, in plain DOM as the flow is. Its
handler opens only the cards it lists. stedding.import.arc_last records that an
import ran and, next, what it did with routes. Settings' Sync and import has
"After moving from Arc" once one has run or while Arc's sidebar is found
(settings T59), and the command bar has "Where Everything from Arc Went"
(commandbar K40).

Why: people from Arc do not find what moved, and a list at the moment of the
move is the one they will read (BACKLOG S-422).

Removable when: never as behaviour; the page may go when nobody comes from Arc.
